1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,479
What is GitHub?

2
00:00:07,033 --> 00:00:13,054
GitHub is a hosting and collaboration platform built around Git repositories.

3
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:17,588
Git does the version control; GitHub adds a shared server,

4
00:00:17,588 --> 00:00:23,530
access control, pull requests, reviews, issues, Actions and releases on top.

5
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:27,518
We talk to a real GitHub repository with plain Git.

6
00:00:29,267 --> 00:00:33,666
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:41,423
Ask GitHub's Git server what a public repository contains, without cloning it:

8
00:00:41,423 --> 00:00:42,257
Clone it:

9
00:00:42,257 --> 00:00:48,369
the same git clone as in lesson 39, with an https://github.com/...

10
00:00:48,369 --> 00:00:48,740
URL.

11
