Repository not found.

75
00:05:35,285 --> 00:05:41,068
Now that Git is authenticated (unlike lesson 44), GitHub says it clearly:

76
00:05:41,068 --> 00:05:47,723
under this owner there is no repository with that name, or you have no access to it.

77
00:05:47,723 --> 00:05:50,971
Compare the remote URL with the page URL:

78
00:05:52,733 --> 00:05:54,533
Here is the fix.

79
00:05:56,267 --> 00:05:56,980
Got it.

80
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:59,731
What do I need to remember?

81
00:06:00,267 --> 00:06:06,471
git remote add origin URL + git push -u origin main publishes a local repository.

82
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:12,878
An authenticated Repository not found means a wrong owner/name or no access.

83
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:17,398
The commit IDs are identical locally and on GitHub.

84
00:06:19,133 --> 00:06:22,488
Why would I need GitHub repository structure?

85
00:06:23,033 --> 00:06:26,948
What each tab of a GitHub repository page is for,

86
00:06:26,948 --> 00:06:30,464
which of them are plain Git (Code, Branches,

87
00:06:30,464 --> 00:06:39,093
Tags) and which are GitHub features stored outside Git (Issues, Pull requests, Actions, Releases, Settings).

88
00:06:39,093 --> 00:06:42,928
For each tab we use the command-line equivalent.

89
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:49,066
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

